# #393 — a live ladder.py appends to these two while a driver runs, and they
# only ever hold the cells THIS machine was given: 37 of the ladder's 40 rows
# on elisa, 36 of the decision log's. collect_results.sh copies each machine's
# copy to results/per_machine/<base>_<machine>.csv and pools every machine into
# results/{ladder,decisions}_all.csv, which are the committed artefacts. A
# 37-row subset sitting at the same level under a shorter name reads like the
# experiment and is not.
experiments/2026-08-04_ema_sched_ladder/results/ladder.csv
experiments/2026-08-04_ema_sched_ladder/results/decisions.csv
